From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sparrow Hawk BSP <bsp@sparrow-hawk>
Date: Wed, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] pta: add W77Q flash dump Pseudo-TA

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BSP-specific W77Q diagnostic support]

Add a Pseudo-TA (w77q_dump.pta) that exposes two commands callable from
Normal World via libteec:

  W77Q_DUMP_CMD_LIST_ALL (0) — enumerate every object in the tee_lfs store
    regardless of owning TA UUID.  Returns packed ts_lut_entry records.

  W77Q_DUMP_CMD_READ_RAW (1) — read raw bytes from the W77Q flash by
    byte offset, bypassing the FS layer.

  W77Q_DUMP_CMD_WRITE_RAW (2) — write raw bytes to W77Q flash (diagnostic).

  W77Q_DUMP_CMD_ERASE_SECTOR (3) — erase the 4 KB sector at a given offset;
    LUT rebuilt from flash afterwards.

  W77Q_DUMP_CMD_ERASE_CHIP (4) — erase all of section 1; reinitialise
    dynamic block and rescan (LUT will be empty).

Both read/write/erase commands call tee_lfs_*() functions defined in
core/tee/tee_lfs_storage.c and compiled unconditionally when CFG_W77Q_FS=y.

Compiled only when CFG_W77Q_DUMP_PTA=y.

Signed-off-by: Sparrow Hawk BSP <bsp@sparrow-hawk>
---
 core/pta/sub.mk              |   4 +
 core/pta/w77q_dump.c         | 186 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 core/include/w77q_dump_ta.h  | 107 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 297 insertions(+)

